{"body":"## Goal

Prove or reject one bounded, task-specific 0.5B path for cnm's bundled offline commit-message generator after unmodified 1B and 2B models failed the frozen quality gate. The pierce must determine whether specialization plus deterministic built-in-style rendering can preserve the complete message contract in a genuinely smaller distribution.

## Maintainer decision

On 2026-07-25 the maintainer rejected increasing the bundled product to approximately 4 GB and confirmed this path instead:

- train one approximately 0.5B model specifically for commit-message generation;
- use code to render the mechanical parts of built-in message styles deterministically;
- keep `auto`, `conventional`, `angular`, `google`, `atom`, `plain`, and `custom`;
- keep additive Custom Guidance, primary `custom` guidance, and multi-line messages;
- keep normal generation fully offline with no API, Ollama, or first-run download;
- cap the complete installed distribution at **700,000,000 bytes** per platform;
- do not begin the Git workflow rewrite unless this pierce passes.

This changes the implementation strategy, not the user-visible message contract.

## Frozen base family

- Base model: `Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-0.5B-Instruct`
- Official revision: `ea3f2471cf1b1f0db85067f1ef93848e38e88c25`
- Parameters: 494,032,768 total / approximately 0.36B non-embedding
- Architecture: Qwen2 causal language model, code-specialized, instruction-tuned
- Context: 32,768 tokens
- License: Apache-2.0
- Training representation: BF16 MLX conversion from the official revision; any conversion must preserve source hashes and tokenizer/template
- Distribution target: fused GGUF, Q5_K_M first; Q6 may be measured as a quality ceiling but is not shippable unless the complete installed tree stays within 700,000,000 bytes
- Runtime: one pinned lightweight llama.cpp build

The official unfine-tuned Q5_K_M is 522,186,624 bytes. That is only a planning reference; the fused artifact and complete installed tree must be measured rather than assumed.

No second base-model family is allowed in this issue. If this base cannot pass after the two allowed training configurations, stop.

## Responsibility split

The model does not have to learn seven complete surface syntaxes. It produces one validated semantic record containing:

- `type`: Conventional/Angular type or null;
- `scope`: concise scope or null;
- `subject`: final semantic subject content;
- `body`: optional final body content.

The wire shape must be grammar-constrained and parseable. A minimal end-to-end renderer then:

- applies Conventional and Angular prefixes and separators;
- joins subject and body with exactly one blank line;
- applies built-in mechanical casing/shape rules;
- rejects empty, malformed, Markdown-wrapped, explanatory, or unparseable output;
- leaves custom subject/body content intact apart from universal safety/shape validation;
- uses recent history for `auto` without allowing copied history to replace diff semantics.

The renderer may guarantee syntax, but it must not invent semantic content or silently repair a materially wrong model summary. The final rendered message, not the intermediate record, is what every quality gate scores.

## Data boundary

Freeze the corpus before training or inspecting high-risk candidate output.

Required properties:

- real, complete multi-file commit diffs and their messages; do not train primarily on single-file slices of multi-file commits;
- repository-isolated train/validation/test splits;
- normalized patch near-duplicate checks against all frozen high-risk and historical evaluation commits;
- source repository, revision, license, diff hash, message hash, and transformation provenance recorded per family;
- secrets and credentials rejected before any external processing;
- strict source-message quality filters and an audited random sample;
- all seven styles represented through the end-to-end renderer;
- diverse Guidance combinations including Chinese, issue references, exact prefixes, subject-only, required body, Why body, SECURITY, and exact bullet counts;
- held-out guidance templates used only for validation/test so the gate measures composition rather than memorized phrases;
- no private project diff is sent to an external labeling service.

Reuse from #31 is allowed only after re-audit. Its 840 direct-output training records are not sufficient evidence and its single-file slices must not silently become full-commit labels.

## Hardware gate

Current training host:

- Apple M5 Pro, 18 CPU cores / 20 GPU cores;
- 48 GB unified memory;
- 367 GiB currently free.

Observed #31 reference:

- Gemma 270M LoRA rank 8;
- max sequence 10,240;
- 1,200 iterations in 222 seconds;
- peak reported memory 19.971 GB.

Before a real run, execute a short training smoke test containing the longest allowed training sequence and record peak memory, swap growth, step time, and loss finiteness.

Continue on this Mac only when:

- the smoke run finishes without OOM or non-finite loss;
- peak process/unified-memory pressure stays at or below 40 GB;
- swap growth attributable to the run stays at or below 2 GB;
- projected run time is practical enough to finish the two bounded configurations.

If this gate fails, stop before full training and prepare a reproducible handoff for the maintainer's RTX 5080 Windows machine. The supported handoff target is WSL2 with pinned NVIDIA/PyTorch training dependencies; do not spend issue scope building a general cross-platform training system.

## Allowed training budget

- At most two predeclared LoRA/SFT configurations.
- Freeze each configuration, seed, tokenizer, sequence cap, optimizer, schedule, rank, targeted layers, checkpoint rule, and data hashes before evaluating its high-risk output.
- Use assistant-output-only loss.
- Select checkpoints only by frozen validation criteria, never by the 26 high-risk cases.
- Evaluate the selected BF16+adapter result first, then the fused Q5_K_M distribution candidate.
- A second configuration may address a diagnosed optimization failure or underfit, but may not change the base family, leak evaluation cases, or begin an open-ended hyperparameter search.
- No full-parameter training, DPO/RL, model merge, RAG, model ensemble, fallback model, or provider abstraction unless a later maintainer decision creates a new issue.

## Risk order and stop conditions

### 1. Data validity and leakage

Pass only when manifests, licenses, splits, near-duplicate checks, transformations, audits, and hashes are complete. Stop if a trustworthy multi-file corpus cannot be assembled within the bounded experiment.

### 2. Hardware smoke

Apply the hardware gate above. A Mac failure is a handoff condition, not evidence that the 0.5B model class failed.

### 3. Frozen end-to-end evaluator

Preserve the same 26 semantic scenarios and real diffs used by #31–#33, but freeze a new bundle hash because the prompt, structured output, parser, and renderer are intentionally different. Run evaluator self-checks proving that malformed records and renderer violations fail.

### 4. Base baseline

Run the unmodified BF16 base through the complete semantic-record and renderer path before training. Record the result for comparison; it is not expected to pass and does not consume a training configuration.

### 5. Selected BF16+LoRA quality

Independent blinded semantic scoring remains 0/1/2:

- `2`: accurate and sufficiently complete, no invented material behavior;
- `1`: materially relevant but incomplete or imprecise;
- `0`: wrong, empty, malformed, code/diff echo, materially invented, or unusable.

Pass only when final rendered output satisfies all of:

- no case scores `0`;
- at least 24/26 score `2`;
- explicit Guidance passes 5/5;
- required-body usefulness passes 4/4;
- Conventional and Angular final formats pass all frozen checks;
- no Markdown wrapper, explanation, repetition, history substitution, or code/diff echo appears.

If neither allowed configuration passes BF16, **STOP**. Do not quantize, run historical evaluation, package a runtime, or implement Git writes.

### 6. Fused Q5_K_M quality

Fuse the selected adapter, convert with pinned tools, quantize to Q5_K_M, and rerun the identical end-to-end gate. It must independently meet every BF16 threshold. Quantization regression is a failure; do not hide it behind the renderer.

### 7. Repeatability and historical quality

Only after Q5 passes:

- rerun all 26 cases in a fresh process with the same seed;
- run a repository-isolated 50–100 commit historical blind review;
- require at least 90% usable historical messages and no critical semantic failure.

### 8. Complete installed size, performance, and offline proof

Only after quality passes:

- measure model, runtime, non-system libraries/resources, launcher, license, and notices;
- require total installed bytes `<= 700,000,000` with no hidden download or package-manager runtime;
- record cold and warm latency, prompt/decode throughput, and peak RSS on the Apple M5 Pro;
- block outbound network access and rerun representative small, largest, style, guidance, and multi-line cases.

## Quality commitments

- **Functional suitability:** final rendered messages must pass the frozen semantic, style, Guidance, body, and historical gates.
- **Performance efficiency:** training hardware is gated before the full run; the complete installed product stays within 700,000,000 bytes; runtime latency/RSS are measured after quality passes.
- **Reliability:** source/model/tool/data/config hashes, repository-isolated splits, fixed seeds, frozen checkpoint selection, and fresh-process reruns make the result reproducible.
- **Security:** normal generation is fully offline; secrets are excluded from data; no private project diff goes to external labeling.
- **Maintainability:** one model, one grammar, one renderer, and one runtime only; no training platform, model registry, or provider layer.

## Out of scope

- Git staging, commit execution, or repository mutation;
- production CLI/TUI implementation;
- changing the seven styles, Custom Guidance, or multi-line contract;
- arbitrary model search or any second base family;
- full-parameter training, preference optimization, RAG, ensembles, or retries through another model;
- runtime model selection, model downloaders, external API/Ollama fallback;
- cross-platform release work before the quality and size gates pass;
- rewriting old product code or documentation beyond Epic status.

## Deliverables

- exact base/conversion/runtime/tool/license manifest and hashes;
- audited, licensed, leakage-checked data manifest and frozen split hashes;
- frozen semantic-record grammar, parser, renderer, evaluator, and corpus hash;
- Mac hardware smoke evidence or reproducible RTX 5080/WSL2 handoff;
- at most two frozen training configs, logs, checkpoints, and selection evidence;
- base, BF16+adapter, and—only after BF16 passes—Q5 raw outputs and independent review;
- if quality passes: repeatability, historical, complete-size, performance/RSS, and offline evidence;
- explicit GO or STOP conclusion;
- Epic writeback.
